<p>The liquidity position of the banking sector is more or less square in the month of April and the surplus funds currently existing in the system will be seen putting a downward pressure on yields in the first fortnight of the next month. The easy liquidity conditions are likely to prompt RBI to announce a gilt issue soon and given the large amount of 364 day treasury bills due for redemption in 1997/98 (82,400 million rupees), a treasury bill conversion is very much on the cards.</p>
<p>The course of interest rate movement over the next three to six months will largely depend upon the Monetary Policy and some strong measures to lower inflation and interest rates should see a strong bull run in bond prices and this time the larger gainers would be the medium and long dated securities.</p>
